implementationPlan.description:
RED first, then two test-only edits in scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs. Nothing else changes: not the bundlers, not moe-jetbrains/build.gradle.kts, not scripts/bundle-manifest.json, and no other row.

RED (test-driven-development): before editing, run the Linux leg of the step-2 command from the worktree root. It must show tests 15, pass 6, fail 9:
- eight rows fail with 'Actual bundler failed: Lockfile <tmp>/packages/moe-daemon/package-lock.json is missing or unreadable';
- the Gradle row fails with 'bundledDaemonDir copy must exclude compiled tests and specs'.
Quote the counts in complete_step. The planning dry run on 5f731334 gave the same 6/9 on Linux node v24.21.0 and on Windows node.exe v24.16.0.

Edit with the Edit tool only. Project rail: no shell writes and no subagent edits to tracked files. The file is LF. A reference diff is at /mnt/d/moe-scratch/a6591f29-plan/fix.diff. Use it to compare only; never git apply it.

Edit A, the fixture (DoD 2, first half). In fixture(), directly after the line `  put(manifestFile, readFileSync(path.join(root, manifestFile)));` (:47 at 5f731334), insert these 7 lines:
```
  // Both bundlers read each package's production set from its lockfile (task-864103f3, task-c76a8bf8) and refuse a
  // missing lockfile or a listed package with no installed package.json.
  for (const name of ['moe-daemon', 'moe-proxy']) {
    put(`packages/${name}/package-lock.json`, JSON.stringify({ name, lockfileVersion: 3, requires: true,
      packages: { '': { name }, 'node_modules/dependency': { version: '0.0.0-fixture' } } }));
    put(`packages/${name}/node_modules/dependency/package.json`, '{"name":"dependency","version":"0.0.0-fixture"}');
  }
```
Placement:
- It follows the governor's comment on this row: separate statements after put(manifestFile, ...).
- Keep the `for (const name of ['moe-agent.ps1', ...])` scripts list exactly as it is, including the 'moe-serena-ignore.mjs' entry that task-c6a24053 landed in 5f731334. Do not reorder, reflow or drop it.
- Leave the existing per-package loop as it is too. Its node_modules/.bin/not-production line is what the exclusion row checks.

Why this shape:
- moe-vscode/scripts/bundle-assets.mjs productionPackages() (:67) reads packages/<pkg>/package-lock.json (asset.lock, :19/:27) and requires a lockfileVersion 2+ `packages` map. It takes every node_modules/<name> key not marked dev: true and refuses link entries.
- bundleProblems() (:118) then requires node_modules/<rel>/package.json to be a file.
- build.gradle.kts productionPackages() applies the same rule.
- One installed production entry, `dependency`, runs the real read-and-copy path. The fixture already writes node_modules/dependency/index.js, so only its package.json is new.

Edit B, the Gradle row (DoD 2, second half). In test('Gradle drops compiled tests from the daemon and proxy dist copies') (:280), directly after its `const source = readFileSync(...)` line, insert:
```
  // The dist copies and the import scan share one list (task-864103f3): check its patterns, then that each copy applies it.
  const list = source.match(/^val distTestExcludes = listOf\(([^)]*)\)$/m)?.[1];
  assert.ok(list, 'Missing Gradle distTestExcludes list');
  const patterns = [...list.matchAll(/"([^"]*)"/g)].map(match => match[1]);
  for (const pattern of ['**/*.test.*', '**/*.spec.*']) assert.ok(patterns.includes(pattern), `distTestExcludes must list ${pattern}`);
```
Then, in the loop (:285), replace `block.includes('exclude("**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*")')` with `block.includes('exclude(distTestExcludes)')`. Keep the assertion message and the block regex unchanged.

What the row now matches in build.gradle.kts:
- :32 declares `val distTestExcludes = listOf("**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*")`.
- The from(bundledDaemonDir) and from(bundledProxyDir) copies (:279-286) apply `exclude(distTestExcludes)`.
- A JS m-flag `$` also matches before a CR, so a CRLF checkout (Windows CI) still matches.

Error handling: no runtime error handling changes. The fixture only supplies inputs the bundler already validates: a missing or malformed lockfile, or an uninstalled entry, is refused with exit 1. The new Gradle assertions fail with named messages, not a TypeError, when the list is absent.

After both edits, re-run the Linux leg: 15 of 15 pass.
